<section id="formulaires">
		<section>
			<h1>Forms</h1>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>Label each field </h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Label is visible</li>
			  <li>Label and fields are connected</li>
			  <li>Label is meaningful and contains all necessary info</li>
			</ul>	
		</section>	
		<section>
			<h2>Placeholder is not enough</h2>
			<img class="stretch" title="" alt="Fields with placeholders, without label. Third field is empty" src="https://images.anysurfer.be/forms/placeholder_sans_label.png">
			<p><a href="http://www.webaxe.org/placeholder-attribute-is-not-a-label/">A placeholder does not replace a label</a></p>
</section>					

<section>
<h2>&lt;label&gt; connected to field</h2>
<p>For attribute of label = id attribute of field</p>
			
<pre><code is:raw data-trim>&lt;label for="name"&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;</code></pre>
			  	<pre><code is:raw data-trim>&lt;input type="text" id="name" /&gt;</code></pre>
			
		
		</section>	
		<section>
			  <h2>Label contains important info</h2>
			  	<ul> 
					<li>date format (dd/mm/jjjj)</li>
					<li>mandatory field (*)</li>
				</ul>

		</section>				
		<section>
			<h2>For fields without visible label</h2>
			<p>Use title attribute or aria-label</p>
			<img class=" stretch" title="" alt="Edit field numéro de compte with tooltip" src="https://images.anysurfer.be/forms/num_compte.png">
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>title attribute - example</h2>
			<p>In a table</p>
			<img class="stretch" title="" alt="Tooltip sur textarea dans tableau: 'Remarque pour vélo Bremshey'" src="https://images.anysurfer.be/forms/tooltip_panier_dachat.png">
		</section>					
					
		<section>
			<h2><code is:raw>fieldset</code> and <code is:raw>legend</code></h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Necessary when <a href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/4.1.4/fieldset_ok2_fr.htm">several fields are grouped and share a label</a></li>
				<li><a href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/4.1.4/fieldset_nok_fr.htm">Don't overuse, keep legend concise</a></li>
				<li><a href="http://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/forms/grouping/">Examples of fieldsets in WAI tutorial</a></li>
			</ul>
		</section>	
		 	<section>
	<h2>Identify input purpose</h2>
	<ul>
	<li>Tells the browser what information is expected.</li>
	<li>Use autocomplete to enable correct autofill, <a href="https://examples.anysurfer.be/forms/form_autocomplete.html">for example</a></li>
	<li>For commonly used information like name, address, email, phone number,...</li>
	<li>Provide fields with an autocomplete attribute when a value for it exists in <a href="http://www.w3.org/TR/html52/sec-forms.html#sec-autofill">HTML5 specification for Autofill</a></li>
	</ul>
	</section>	
		<section>
	<pre><code is:raw>
	&lt;label for="name"&gt;Last name&lt;/label&gt;
	&lt;input autocomplete="family-name" type="text" id="name" name="name" /&gt;
	</code></pre>
	</section>
	
	<section>
	<pre><code is:raw>
	&lt;label for="country"&gt;Country&lt;/label&gt;
	&lt;input autocomplete="country" type="text" id="country" name="country" /&gt;
	</code></pre>
	
	</section>
	
	<section>
		<h2></h2>
	<h2>Spam protection</h2>
	<ul>
	<li>Don't ask user to copy a set of characters (captcha)</li>
	<li>Alternatives: time analysis, honeypot, email, text-verification,...</li>
	<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/turingtest/">Inaccessibility of CAPTCHA: alternatives to visual Turing tests on the web</a></li>
	</ul>
	</section>
	
	<section>
		<h2>Form validation</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Every form must have a send button</li>
			<li>Make error messages easy to find (focus management)</li>
			<li>Describe error and mention the corresponding field</li>
			<li>Combine with visual cues (color, icons)</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
	
		<section>
		<h2>And also</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Semantics: use native form elements</li>
				<li>reading order: put important information at the beginning</li>
				<li>Color: avoid 'errors are shown in orange'</li>
				<li>Label positioning: think about small screens and people using zoom</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</section>
